**PHASE 1 — Foundation**

1. 🌱 What is Jetpack Compose?
 - Jetpack Compose is a declarative UI framework.
 - Instead of writing XML layouts, you describe the UI in Kotlin code.
 - It automatically updates the UI when the data changes (reactive programming).

In XML:

<TextView
    android:text="Hello World"
    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
    android:layout_height="wrap_content"/>

In Compose:

@Composable
fun Greeting() {
    Text(text = "Hello World")
}

 - @Composable - Tells the compiler that this function is for UI.
 - Composables can call other composables.

**Modifier**
 - Used to customize composables → size, padding, background, click, shape, etc.
 - Example:
 Text(
     text = "Nirbhay",
     modifier = Modifier
         .padding(16.dp)
         .background(Color.Yellow)
         .fillMaxWidth()
         .clickable { Log.d("TAG", "Text clicked!") }
 )

 ** Modifier.fillMaxSize()
  - It tells the Composable to expand and take up all the available space of its parent (both width and height).
  - Just like match_parent in xml on both height and width
